IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 109 of 2022
CITATION: 2021 SCC OnLine SC 941
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Sanjay Kishan Kaul, M.M. Sundresh

PARTIES:
Aman Preet Singh vs CBI

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 170 CrPC, Section 437 CrPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
custody on chargesheet, custody not mandatory, cooperation in investigation

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that trial courts cannot mechanically insist on remanding an accused to custody merely because a chargesheet has been submitted under Section 170 CrPC if they cooperated throughout investigation.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 170 CrPC, Section 437 CrPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

